<title>ESTONIA: MOODY'S A LIKELY CANDIDATE FOR RATING-C.BANK.</title>
<headline>MOODY'S A LIKELY CANDIDATE FOR RATING-C.BANK.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonia's central bank on Tuesday denied local media reports that it had chosen Moody's as the agency to assign a rating to the country but said that Moody's topped its list of candidates.</p>
<p>Local media reported on Monday that the central bank had decided to order the credit rating from Moody's, quoting a banking source.</p>
<p>&quot;Moody's is a likely candidate with whom we have contacts,&quot; the central bank's spokesperson told Reuters.</p>
<p>The spokesperson added that the bank was also considering two or three other agencies.</p>
<p>Moody's assigned a rating Ba2 rating to Lithuania's foreign currency debt last year and a Ba3 to the country's bank deposits. That was the first credit rating granted to a former Soviet republic.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
